# Running HART

The runner is:

```text
scripts/reproduce_legacy_posid.py
```

Method selection uses:

```text
--methods
```

Supported methods:

```text
re_posid
wordnet_posid
re_wordnet_posid
word2vec_posid
sbert_posid
re_sbert_posid
```

Subset selection uses:

```text
--subset
```

Relevant subsets:

```text
full
non_generated_28
non_generated_plus_generated_58
generated_only
generated_flash_only
```

The important 58-document slice is:

```text
10 Synthetic
13 Press Release
5 Incident Reports
30 Generated
= 58
```

It excludes all 500 `Generated_flash` documents.

Run the non-SBERT methods on the 58-doc slice:

```bash
python scripts/reproduce_legacy_posid.py \
  --incitext-root ../InciText \
  --output-dir outputs/legacy_reproduction_58 \
  --subset non_generated_plus_generated_58 \
  --methods re_posid word2vec_posid wordnet_posid re_wordnet_posid
```

Run the zero-shot methods separately:

```bash
python scripts/reproduce_legacy_posid.py \
  --incitext-root ../InciText \
  --output-dir outputs/legacy_reproduction_58_sbert \
  --subset non_generated_plus_generated_58 \
  --methods sbert_posid re_sbert_posid
```

Use separate output directories so one run does not overwrite another.

